cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the relevant manuscript and this repository."
title: "Topological-Index Pilot: Wuzi index family and orthogonality-screening pipeline for QSPR"
authors:
  - family-names: "Natarajan"
    given-names: "Advik"
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics, Loyola College, Chennai"
  - family-names: "Shiwakoti"
    given-names: "Ganesh"
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics and Statistics, Florida Atlantic University"
    email: "ganshiwakoti@gmail.com"
  - family-names: "Arockiaraj"
    given-names: "Michael"
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics, Loyola College, Chennai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Singati2/topological-index-orthogonality"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - "topological indices"
  - "Wuzi index family"
  - "bond-incident-degree"
  - "ratio-bound theorem"
  - "extremal graphs"
  - "QSPR"
  - "orthogonality screening"
  - "cheminformatics"
abstract: >-
  Companion software for two manuscripts.

  Paper 1 (Wuzi index family): graph-theoretic properties, closed-form
  values on standard graph classes, a rigorous ratio-bound theorem with
  respect to classical bond-incident-degree (BID) indices, a
  computational extremal-tree study, and a sensitivity analysis on the
  18 octanes, 106 trees of order 10, and 75 decane isomers.

  Paper 2 (orthogonality-screening pipeline): an open-source pipeline
  combining pairwise correlation, principal-component (PCA) effective
  rank, partial correlation with the target, variance inflation factor
  (VIF), and a combined criterion, applied to a 30-index classical
  baseline on the ESOL, FreeSolv, Lipophilicity, and BBBP datasets,
  together with a 5-fold cross-validated RandomForest benchmark.
version: "1.7.0"
date-released: "2026-05-25"
